## Context / Problem
RP-05 replaces repeated CLI censuses with shared route/capability authority, intentionally normalizes help for 21 commands, and makes parser-derived generated help a public compatibility boundary. These are structural decisions with migration and rollback consequences, so the rationale must land before implementation.

Research is durable on `rubellite-secondary-cub` and in `.joe-janitor/rp05-cli-registry-research.md`. It covers current source/tests/history plus CPython argparse, Django, Click, Cobra, pip, and Git conventions. The maintainer approved the design; approval of the exact ADR draft remains a separate HOLD decision.

## Approach
Create the ADR (allocated as 0100; 0099 was already taken by the landed binding-store ADR) using repository ADR numbering/index machinery. Record:

- one stdlib-only immutable top-level route registry with lazy handler and parser-factory `module:function` references and bounded invocation adapters;
- side-effect-free stdlib argparse factories as the single grammar source for runtime parsing and generated syntax/options;
- deterministic fixed-`prog`/width/formatter generation of committed runtime-authoritative package help and grouped overview;
- the distinction between the tiny lexical top-level selector and selected-handler argument parsing, with no second parser or docs DSL;
- one semantic capability registry with `error`, `unavailable`, `abstain`, and intentional `fallback` postures;
- pre-operation help/alias/unknown routing before RP-04 snapshot, config, mount, handlers, or optional imports;
- canonical/exact/compatibility/hidden/retired alias rules, including shared argument-definition helpers for bridge shims and historical `jira-onboard`;
- curated prose/examples as editorial supplements only, never an unchecked syntax authority;
- build-time factory resolution versus lean runtime help, full-extra validation, and no eager optional imports;
- expand/contract migration by command family, parity oracles, generated-artifact cutover, and code-only rollback;
- explicit non-goals: no plugin framework, Click dependency, DI container, middleware framework, MCP-as-verb, or stored-data change.

Update `docs/architecture.md` only with the implemented boundary and link. Regenerate `docs/adr/README.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/0100`; do not hand-edit generated artifacts.

## Architecture Decision Lifecycle
The research summary is on `rubellite-secondary-cub`. Before drafting, post the numbered research critique: unverified assumptions, dependencies not investigated, unanswered questions, and conflicts with ADR 0098 or existing CLI ADRs. Resolve every item. Draft from verified findings, run the draft critique, and submit through Gerrit in HOLD. No implementation child starts until the exact draft receives explicit maintainer approval, both Gerrit gates pass, and the ADR lands.

0099 was no longer free after refreshing `origin/main` (taken by the landed binding-store ADR), so the lowest unused number 0100 was allocated with `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`, this ticket's file impact was updated to 0100 before review/claim, and the approved slug was preserved.

## Testing
The document oracle is the ADR-number bijection plus byte-current generated index. The architecture oracle is a cross-check against the approved research, parser/runtime same-source decision, current help/mount/output contracts, and RP-04 ADR 0098.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [x] The ADR cites the approved research and maintained-project sources and records every parser, generation, route, help, alias, capability, validation, scope-limit, migration, and rollback decision without contradicting ADR 0098.
- [x] The ADR explicitly prohibits docs-only grammars and requires each parser-family migration to switch runtime and tests with its factory before generated help becomes authoritative.
- [x] `docs/architecture.md` describes the implemented CLI boundary and links ADR 0100 without copying historical rationale.
- [x] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` verify the ADR file, marker, generated index, and links.
- [x] [operator-attested] The exact ADR draft receives explicit maintainer approval after its draft critique and before Gerrit Submit.
